Package: signsrv
Version: 0.0.2-0
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: stevekieu <msh.computing@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE_KB@
Depends: adduser, init-system-helpers (>= 1.54)
Recommends: logrotate, openssl
Section: web
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/sunshine69/pdf-go
Description: PDF signing service with evidential signatures
 signsrv fills a PDF form, invites the signers by email with expiring single-use
 links, records each consent as a signature, signs the document once everyone has
 consented, verifies the result, and delivers it to every party.
 .
 Signatures are PKCS#7 / CAdES-BES with an RFC 3161 timestamp, so a document
 certifies its own integrity and every consent is bound to a person by an
 irrevocable token. A verification needs only the document: no database, no
 account, and no network.
 .
 This package installs the service, a systemd unit, and the first-boot setup that
 creates the state directories, the CA keystore and the database schema, then starts
 the service. A reverse proxy (nginx or Caddy) terminating TLS in front of the
 loopback listener is required to serve the public signing pages.
